    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1a118909-17ad-5290-a0db-925c009e6c01",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ is a solution of $Ax=0$?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$ A\\text{ is invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{4} \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)&=4 \\\\ \\text{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A)&=0\\end{aligned}\\right. $$\n\nSince $v\\ne 0$ and $Av=0$, the nullspace contains a nonzero vector. Thus $A$ is not invertible. This does not determine its exact rank or nullity.\n\nWe have $\\text{rank}(A)<4$, $\\text{nullity}(A)>0$, $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne\\{0\\}$, and $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne\\mathbb{R}^{4}$.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false: $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$. Compare this statement with the consequences above.\n\n- Statement II is true: $A is not invertible$. Compare this statement with the consequences above.\n\n- Statement III is false: $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4}$. Compare this statement with the consequences above.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is II only.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
